    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d395">

                <pb facs="0482" n="402" sameAs="frus:frus1930v01/pg402"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">863.51 Relief Credits/234</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Edge</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-05-23">May 23, 1930</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 170</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your despatch
                    No. 517, dated May 2, 1930,<anchor n="16" xml:id="d395-f1"/> transmitting the
                    reply of the French Government to the Embassy’s inquiry regarding the Austrian
                    loan pursuant to the Department’s cabled instruction No. 93 of April 15, 6 p.m.,
                    to the Embassy at London.</p>
                <p>The reply of the French Government is not directly responsive to the Department’s
                    inquiry on behalf of the Treasury Department. The Embassy is requested to
                    endeavor to obtain from the French Government a statement in substance that Sir
                    Frederick Leith-Ross’ letter of April 16, 1930, to the Austrian Minister at
                    London is approved by the French Government and was made pursuant to its
                    authority.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis
                            White</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d395-f1" n="16" xml:id="d395-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; see telegram No. 126, May 2, 4 p.m., from the Ambassador in France,
                        <ref target="#pg399">p. 399</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
